%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: luke&habermas
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: "According to J\xFCrgen Habermas, which fundamental human interest
      is associated with technical knowledge and empirical-analytical sciences?"
    Options:
    - Practical Interest
    - Emancipatory Interest
    - Technical Interest
    - Interpretive Interest
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Allan Luke''s work is most centrally concerned with the relationship
      between literacy education and:'
    Options:
    - Cognitive psychology
    - Power and social inequality
    - Phonetic awareness
    - Standardized testing
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s "practical interest" is oriented toward:'
    Options:
    - Prediction and control of the environment
    - Mutual understanding and hermeneutic interpretation
    - Liberation from oppressive social structures
    - Technical efficiency in teaching
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Critical literacy, as advocated by Allan Luke, primarily aims
      to:'
    Options:
    - Improve students' reading speed and comprehension
    - Teach students to decode texts without questioning them
    - Enable students to analyze how texts construct and maintain power relations
    - Focus exclusively on classical literature
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s "emancipatory interest" seeks knowledge that leads
      to:'
    Options:
    - Greater technical control over nature
    - Deeper understanding of historical traditions
    - More efficient classroom management
    - Freedom from domination and self-determination
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'According to Luke, a "technocratic" model of teacher education
      focuses primarily on developing:'
    Options:
    - Critical consciousness
    - Political activism
    - Technical skills and competencies
    - Cultural sensitivity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory of "knowledge-constitutive interests" suggests
      that all knowledge is:'
    Options:
    - Value-neutral and objective
    - Socially constructed and interest-bound
    - Based solely on sensory experience
    - Independent of human purposes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke argues that the "Four Resources Model" of literacy includes
      all EXCEPT:'
    Options:
    - Code-breaker
    - Text-participant
    - Text-user
    - Text-memorizer
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: From a Habermasian perspective, a teacher education program focused
      solely on test scores and measurable outcomes is serving which knowledge interest?
    Options:
    - Emancipatory
    - Practical
    - Technical
    - Interpretive
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Allan Luke''s concept of "digital literacies" emphasizes:'
    Options:
    - Learning to use computers without critical analysis
    - The technical skills of coding and programming
    - Critical engagement with how digital texts shape identity and society
    - Avoiding traditional print literacy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program that emphasizes Habermas''s "practical
      interest" would likely focus on developing teachers'' capacity for:'
    Options:
    - Standardized test preparation
    - Dialogic communication and interpretive understanding
    - Behavioral management techniques
    - Political organizing
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s critique of traditional literacy education argues that
      it often:'
    Options:
    - Overemphasizes critical thinking
    - Neglects phonics instruction
    - Focuses too much on social justice
    - Fails to address issues of power and ideology in texts
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s "ideal speech situation" requires the absence of:'
    Options:
    - Disagreement
    - Systematic distortion of communication
    - Technical terminology
    - Cultural differences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'According to Luke, effective literacy teachers need knowledge
      of:'
    Options:
    - Only phonics and grammar
    - The sociocultural and political contexts of literacy practices
    - Literary classics exclusively
    - Computer programming
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: From a Habermasian perspective, action research in teacher education
      primarily serves which knowledge interest?
    Options:
    - Technical
    - Practical
    - Emancipatory
    - Regulatory
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s work in critical policy analysis examines how educational
      policies often:'
    Options:
    - Promote social equality effectively
    - Serve dominant economic and political interests
    - Are developed through democratic consensus
    - Focus exclusively on academic achievement
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s concept of the "lifeworld" being "colonized" by the
      "system" refers to:'
    Options:
    - The invasion of personal life by technological systems
    - The domination of communicative action by instrumental rationality
    - The spread of literacy throughout society
    - The biological colonization of ecosystems
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher using Luke''s critical literacy approach would encourage
      students to:'
    Options:
    - Memorize textbook content accurately
    - Avoid controversial topics in the classroom
    - Focus solely on literal comprehension
    - Question whose interests are served by particular texts
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory suggests that teacher knowledge should include
      understanding of how to foster:'
    Options:
    - Unquestioning acceptance of authority
    - Critical self-reflection and democratic discourse
    - Technical efficiency in learning
    - Traditional cultural values
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke argues that curriculum should be understood as:'
    Options:
    - A neutral document for organizing content
    - Primarily a teacher's guide
    - A fixed sequence of learning objectives
    - A culturally and politically contested space
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program informed by Habermas''s emancipatory
      interest would prioritize:'
    Options:
    - Standardized teaching methods
    - Developing teachers' capacity for critical reflection on social structures
    - Technical classroom management skills
    - Content knowledge exclusively
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s "Four Resources Model" positions literacy as:'
    Options:
    - A simple decoding process
    - A sociocultural practice involving multiple roles
    - Primarily about literary appreciation
    - A technical skill separate from culture
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: From a Habermasian perspective, the current emphasis on "evidence-based
      practice" in education primarily reflects which knowledge interest?
    Options:
    - Emancipatory
    - Practical
    - Technical
    - Aesthetic
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s work on globalization and education emphasizes the need
      for teachers to understand:'
    Options:
    - Only local educational contexts
    - How global economic forces shape local educational practices
    - Standardized international curricula
    - The elimination of cultural differences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory of communicative action emphasizes the importance
      of:'
    Options:
    - Strategic action for success
    - Individual competitive achievement
    - Technical control of educational outcomes
    - Reaching understanding through dialogue
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A critical literacy classroom, following Luke''s approach, would
      likely engage students in:'
    Options:
    - Rote memorization of texts
    - Analyzing how texts position readers and construct reality
    - Avoiding all political content
    - Focusing only on personal responses to literature
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s knowledge-constitutive interests theory suggests that
      teacher education has been dominated by:'
    Options:
    - Emancipatory interests
    - Practical and technical interests equally
    - Technical interests at the expense of others
    - Aesthetic interests
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke argues that multicultural education often fails when it:'
    Options:
    - Includes too many perspectives
    - Becomes a superficial celebration of diversity without addressing power relations
    - Focuses on structural inequality
    - Emphasizes critical literacy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: From a Habermasian perspective, a curriculum focused on developing
      students' moral reasoning would serve which knowledge interest?
    Options:
    - Technical
    - Instrumental
    - Emancipatory
    - Practical
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s concept of "literacy as social practice" suggests that
      reading and writing are always:'
    Options:
    - Individual psychological processes
    - Embedded in cultural and power relations
    - Separate from social contexts
    - Universal skills with fixed meanings
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program truly integrating Habermas''s three
      knowledge interests would balance focus on:'
    Options:
    - Skills, understanding, and liberation
    - Content, pedagogy, and assessment
    - Theory, practice, and research
    - Individual, community, and global perspectives
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s critique of educational reform movements suggests they
      often:'
    Options:
    - Adequately address issues of power
    - Reinforce existing inequalities through new means
    - Successfully achieve educational equity
    - Focus too much on critical theory
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s work provides a foundation for understanding teacher
      research as:'
    Options:
    - Only quantitative measurement
    - A means for technical control of learning
    - A process of critical self-reflection and social transformation
    - Unrelated to classroom practice
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'According to Luke, effective teacher development requires:'
    Options:
    - Isolated technical training
    - Engagement with the political dimensions of teaching
    - Avoidance of controversial topics
    - Focus only on classroom management
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory suggests that the current emphasis on standardized
      testing in teacher education reflects:'
    Options:
    - An emancipatory interest
    - Balanced attention to all knowledge interests
    - A practical interest in understanding
    - The colonization of education by system imperatives
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s work on indigenous education emphasizes the importance
      of:'
    Options:
    - Assimilating indigenous students into mainstream culture
    - Recognizing epistemological diversity and challenging colonial knowledge systems
    - Teaching only Western knowledge systems
    - Avoiding cultural content in curriculum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A Habermasian approach to teacher professional development would
      prioritize:'
    Options:
    - One-way transmission of expert knowledge
    - Standardized performance metrics
    - Individual competitive improvement
    - Dialogic communities of practice
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke argues that the knowledge base for teaching must include
      understanding of how:'
    Options:
    - To implement curriculum without questioning it
    - Knowledge is produced, distributed, and legitimated in society
    - To avoid political issues in the classroom
    - To focus exclusively on academic content
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'From a Habermasian perspective, the most valid form of educational
      knowledge is that which:'
    Options:
    - Has the strongest empirical evidence
    - Produces the highest test scores
    - Is determined by educational authorities
    - Emerges from free and equal dialogue among stakeholders
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s concept of "redesign" in multiliteracies refers to:'
    Options:
    - Making minor adjustments to existing texts
    - The transformative potential of recreating texts for new purposes
    - The technical aspects of text design
    - Standardizing text formats
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education curriculum informed by both Luke and Habermas
      would likely emphasize:'
    Options:
    - Technical skills divorced from social context
    - Isolation of education from social concerns
    - Unquestioning implementation of official curriculum
    - Critical engagement with knowledge and power relations
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory helps explain why teacher education often emphasizes
      technical knowledge because:'
    Options:
    - It is the most important knowledge form
    - It serves system needs for measurable outcomes
    - Teachers prefer technical knowledge
    - It is the easiest to teach
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s work suggests that literacy education reform requires:'
    Options:
    - Better phonics programs
    - Eliminating critical perspectives
    - More standardized testing
    - Addressing broader social and political structures
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'From a Habermasian perspective, the knowledge base for teaching
      should enable teachers to:'
    Options:
    - Efficiently implement prescribed methods
    - Facilitate democratic classroom discourse
    - Control student behavior effectively
    - Maximize test scores reliably
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s analysis of textbook publishing shows how:'
    Options:
    - Texts are neutral carriers of information
    - Commercial interests shape educational knowledge
    - Teachers have complete control over text selection
    - Texts reflect student interests accurately
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher applying Habermas''s principles would prioritize classroom
      activities that:'
    Options:
    - Maximize individual competition
    - Develop technical skills efficiently
    - Foster mutual understanding and critical reflection
    - Prepare students for standardized tests
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke argues that the current crisis in education is fundamentally
      a crisis of:'
    Options:
    - Teacher quality
    - Funding
    - Educational legitimacy and public trust
    - Technological integration
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Habermas''s theory provides a framework for understanding how
      teacher knowledge can serve:'
    Options:
    - Only individual advancement
    - Both system maintenance and social transformation
    - Only technical control
    - Political indoctrination
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
  - QuestionText: 'Luke''s work on Asian education systems challenges Western assumptions
      by showing:'
    Options:
    - The superiority of Asian educational models
    - The complexity and specificity of different educational traditions
    - The need to adopt Asian methods universally
    - The irrelevance of cultural context to education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: luke&habermas
